  "label": "User projected onto the man in the image via the pronoun 'me'",
  "description": "The text overlay 'my wife threw me out after she caught me measuring my cock' explicitly uses the first-person pronoun 'me', which directly projects the user (the viewer of the meme) onto the visual entity 'man'. The man is the only human subject in the image, and the text explicitly identifies him as 'me' in the narrative. This creates a direct semiotic projection where the user is mapped onto the man as the speaker of the text.",
